d`): every row names its production call site and driving\n100|test. The ratio stays **18 of 18 AC rows driven**; no matrix row\n101|changed because the candidate code is unchanged.\n102|\n103|## Validation reran in rev5b (this run, final tree, base `a12d1bd`)\n104|\n105|- Commands 1-3 (`gofmt` check, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`):\n106|  exit 0 (`cmd01.log`, `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n107|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1 -v`): exit 0, 21967 passes,\n108|  38 packages ok, zero `^FAIL` and zero `--- FAIL`\n109|  (`cmd04.log`; the FAIL-text lines inside are nested mutant-kill\n110|  output of the passing `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled`)\n111|- Command 5 (`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`): exit 0,\n112|  38 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE` lines\n113|  (`ok internal/sessquery 390.347s`, `ok internal/clonebundle\n114|  3.172s`) (`cmd05.log`)\n115|- Command 6 (`go test ./... -cover -count=1`): exit 0, 38 packages\n116|  ok — the command that failed the first rev5 construction on the\n117|  trunk time-bomb now passes with the `a12d1bd` fix\n118|  (`ok internal/resumesmoke`, `ok internal/clonebundle 87.1%`)\n119|  (`cmd06.log`)\n120|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): exit 0\n121|  (`cmd07.log` … `cmd20.log`)\n122|- Command 21 (`tracecheck`): exit 0, bindings=68,\n123|  clauses 49/569 — unchanged, `internal/traceability` untouched\n124|  (`cmd21.log`)\n125|- Command 22 (`cataloggen -adopted -check`): exit 0, empty output\n126|  (`cmd22.log`)\n127|- Commands 23-24 (`GOOS=linux/windows` builds): exit 0\n128|  (`cmd23.log`, `cmd24.log`)\n129|- Commands 25-27 (JSON validation, `task-board validate`,\n130|  `git diff --check`): exit 0 (`cmd25.log`, `cmd26.log`,\n131|  `cmd27.log`)\n132|- Package suite: exit 0 (`pkg-test.log`), 87.1% statements\n133|  (`pkg-cover.log`); package race exit 0 (`pkg-race.log`)\n134|- Mutant harness: 67/67 ok (66 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control),\n135|  full battery run twice with per-plant raw logs carrying\n136|  subprocess exits (`mutants/run1/*.log`,\n137|  `mutants/run2/*.log`, `mutants-run1.log`, `mutants-run2.log`),\n138|  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`, tree restored\n139|  (`git status` unchanged after both runs)\n140|\n141|- No `internal/traceability` edit; `git status` shows only\n142|  candidate paths (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n143|  `?? internal/clonebundle/`)\n144|\n145|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n146|\n147|- Per-kind event payload fact registries: which facts a kind may\n148|  carry (normalization sibling). The §1.6 value model on every\n149|  payload member is enforced here, not bounded away.\n150|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n151|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n152|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n153|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`).\n154|- `-0` admits (JCS `0`); `+n`/leading-zero literals refuse at the\n155|  frame gate (stated, not waived).\n156|- Custom-`MarshalJSON` extension values: the text walk trusts the\n157|  computed form (stated, not waived).\n158|- `internal/traceability` bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n159|\n160|## Attachments\n161|\n162|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5, re-executed)\n163|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (rev5b logs:\n164|  27-command suite, package suite, 2×66+1 mutant battery with\n165|  per-plant logs, P3-b probe log, file manifest)","final_result":true}}}
