{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":448,"recorded_at":1780531400000891,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96"},"task_id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(10321 line(s) above)\n10322|### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\n10323|\n10324|A clone is a derivation, never a move or fork alias. It MUST leave source\n10325|bytes, Session Record, provider ID, lease, workspace authority, task-board\n10326|binding, and native identity unchanged. It creates one new direct Session\n10327|Record 2.0.0, target workspace identity, native identity, and epoch-1 lease.\n10328|The target accepts no input until transaction, target Checkpoint, lineage, and\n10329|optional ordinary resume validation succeed.\n10330|\n10331|#### 13.14.1 Capture and canonical contracts\n10332|\n10333|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains its\n10334|schema/version/omission-rule ID, operation ID, source Environment Tuple, and\n10335|sorted unique entries. Each entry has sanitized native\n10336|key, capture class, byte count, blob ID, Blob Descriptor ID, and extensions.\n10337|It contains no credential, runtime, lock, target, AX lease, or fabricated AX\n10338|Session/Provider identity.\n10339|\n10340|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version/ID,\n10341|operation/bundle, source basis, source Environment Tuple, sanitized Native\n10342|Identity, capture-plan digest, Capture Boundary, Raw Object Manifest ID,\n10343|sorted Capture Items, exact excluded classes, core-derived\n10344|<code>raw_complete</code>, creator/time, and extensions. Source basis is\n10345|<code>ax_session</code> with source Session/Record/Checkpoint/Provider Identity\n10346|IDs or <code>external_native</code> with a sanitized source reference.\n10347|\n10348|Each Capture Item has one native key and class\n10349|<code>durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>.\n10350|It is <code>included</code> with descriptor/count and no reason, or\n10351|<code>excluded</code> with null content fields and a stable reason. Credential,\n10352|auth, runtime, and lock classes are excluded. Unknown makes raw completeness\n10353|false and blocks maximal-safe.\n10354|\n10355|Capture Boundary is <code>stable</code> with Stable Snapshot Proof, or\n10356|<code>unstable_archive</code> with generation, pre/post digests,\n10357|<code>source_not_quiescent</code>, explicit acknowledgement, and\n10358|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>. Stable proof records\n10359|<code>closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10360|generation, optional immutable identity, equal pre/post digests, and\n10361|input/foreground/background idle facts. Size equality is never proof. The\n10362|unstable form is core-created only for archive-only output and cannot enter a\n10363|target branch.\n10364|\n10365|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10366|logical Session UUIDv7, source Environment Tuple/native ID, nullable title,\n10367|closed Workspace Binding, 1..1024 Actors, 1..1,000,000 ordered unique Event\n10368|IDs, 1..1024 head IDs, nullable source created/updated times, and extensions.\n10369|Actor contains exactly actor UUIDv7, <code>main|subagent|external</code>,\n10370|nullable parent (null only for main), nullable name/source-native ID/model, and\n10371|extensions.\n10372|\n10373|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10374|logical Session UUIDv7, zero-based contiguous ordinal, 0..64 sorted unique\n10375|causal parents, Actor UUIDv7, nullable turn UUIDv7, kind, nullable source time,\n10376|<code>public|projection|internal|opaque</code> visibility, kind-selected closed\n10377|payload, Source Evidence, and extensions. Source Evidence contains environment\n10378|and native Session IDs, nullable native Event ID/type, sorted unique raw\n10379|blob/manifest byte-range references,\n10380|<code>exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code> capture status, and stable\n10381|reason codes. Synthesized events have no native Event ID and identify the core\n10382|operation.\n10383|\n10384|The exact event kinds are\n10385|<code>session_started|instruction_snapshot|user_message|assistant_message|reasoning_summary|opaque_reasoning|tool_definition_snapshot|tool_call|tool_result|approval_request|approval_response|plan_update|progress|usage|rate_limit|file_change|compaction|turn_started|turn_completed|turn_aborted|subagent_started|subagent_completed|error|migration_checkpoint|session_finished|opaque_event</code>.\n10386|Payloads contain only their registered typed facts. Message-like payloads use\n10387|exactly <code>text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque</code>\n10388|content blocks with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references; inline\n10389|content is at most 64 KiB. Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque\n10390|events. Historical tools\n10391|are inert; incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action.\n10392|Foreign instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\n10393|reasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target accounting.\n10394|\n10395|The following closed shapes govern this subsection; the preceding prose is a\n10396|summary and does not permit omitted or additional members.\n10397|\n10398|<code>NativeIdentity</code> contains exactly\n10399|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10400|<code>identity_kind:provider_native|official_import|continuation_context</code>,\n10401|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10402|<code>backend_realm_fingerprint:digest|null</code>,\n10403|<code>opaque_identity:string[1..512]|null</code>, and\n10404|<code>extensions</code>. It contains no credential, absolute source path as\n10405|cross-host identity, PID, socket, token, or secret environment value.\n10406|\n10407|<code>WorkspaceBinding</code> contains exactly\n10408|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10409|<code>cwd_relative:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10410|<code>repository_remote_fingerprints:sorted unique digest[0..128]</code>,\n10411|<code>branch:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10412|<code>head_digest:digest|null</code>, <code>index_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10413|<code>working_tree_digest:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10414|The relative cwd is normalized beneath the Workspace Group root; no member\n10415|grants filesystem authority.\n10416|\n10417|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10418|\n10419|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10420|| --- | --- |\n10421|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-raw-object-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10422|| <code>raw_object_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10423|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation |\n10424|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact probed <code>EnvironmentTuple</code> |\n10425|| <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Sanitized string[1..512], never an AX Session ID |\n10426|| <code>source_identity_digest</code> | Terminal digest of canonical sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> bytes |\n10427|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Exact core-validated capture-plan digest |\n10428|| <code>entries</code> | <code>RawObjectEntry[0..65536]</code>, sorted unique by native item key |\n10429|| <code>total_bytes</code> | uint53 equal to the sum of entry byte counts |\n10430|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys with no normative reference |\n10431|\n10432|<code>RawObjectEntry</code> contains exactly\n10433|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10434|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|unknown</code>,\n10435|<code>byte_count:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, and\n10436|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>. The descriptor agrees with blob ID and\n10437|byte count. Credential, machine-auth, runtime-state, transient-lock, and\n10438|excluded candidates are forbidden.\n10439|\n10440|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10441|\n10442|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10443|| --- | --- |\n10444|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-capture-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10445|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10446|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation / logical bundle chain |\n10447|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Capture Source Basis below |\n10448|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_identity</code> | Exact tuple / sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> |\n10449|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Terminal digest of the complete canonical capture-plan success body |\n10450|| <code>capture_boundary</code> | Closed Capture Boundary below |\n10451|| <code>source_raw_object_manifest_id</code> | Exact raw manifest containing all and only included objects |\n10452|| <code>items</code> | <code>CaptureItem[0..65536]</code>, sorted bytewise by native item key; one per plan candidate |\n10453|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | Sorted unique capture-class[0..9], exactly the excluded-row classes |\n10454|| <code>raw_complete</code> | Core-derived boolean; true only after complete plan/object reconciliation |\n10455|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> / <code>created_at</code> | UUIDv7 / diagnostic timestamp |\n10456|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10457|\n10458|Capture Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_session</code> contains\n10459|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10460|<code>source_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n10461|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10462|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, and\n10463|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=external_native</code> contains exactly\n10464|<code>kind</code>, <code>external_source_ref:string[1..512]</code>, and\n10465|<code>extensions</code>.\n10466|\n10467|<code>CaptureItem</code> contains exactly\n10468|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10469|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>,\n10470|<code>disposition:included|excluded</code>,\n10471|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest|null</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n10472|<code>exclusion_reason:string[1..128]|null</code>, and\n10473|<code>extensions</code>. Included requires both content members non-null and a\n10474|null reason. Excluded requires null content members and a non-null reason.\n10475|Credential, auth, runtime, and lock classes are always excluded. Unknown makes\n10476|<code>raw_complete=false</code> and blocks <code>maximal_safe</code>.\n10477|\n10478|Capture Boundary is a closed union. <code>kind=stable</code> contains exactly\n10479|<code>kind</code>, <code>proof:StableSnapshotProof</code>, and\n10480|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=unstable_archive</code> contains exactly\n10481|<code>kind</code>, <code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10482|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10483|<code>reason_code=source_not_quiescent</code>,\n10484|<code>operator_explicit=true</code>,\n10485|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10486|Only core may construct the unstable archive form; G2 always rejects it.\n10487|\n10488|<code>StableSnapshotProof</code> contains exactly\n10489|<code>proof_kind:closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10490|<code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10491|<code>snapshot_identity_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10492|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10493|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n10494|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Capture\n10495|digests are equal. Closed-store/provider-quiescence requires all booleans true\n10496|and null snapshot identity; immutable-snapshot/log-prefix requires non-null\n10497|identity. File-size equality is never proof.\n10498|\n10499|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10500|\n10501|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10502|| --- | --- |\n10503|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:canonical-session</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10504|| <code>canonical_session_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10505|| <code>logical_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 stable within bundle lineage |\n10506|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Exact tuple / string[1..512] |\n10507|| <code>title</code> | string[1..4096] or null |\n10508|| <code>workspace</code> | Closed <code>WorkspaceBinding</code> |\n10509|| <code>actors</code> | <code>Actor[1..1024]</code>, unique by actor ID |\n10510|| <code>event_ids</code> | Ordered unique digest[1..1000000] |\n10511|| <code>head_event_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[1..1024], all in event IDs |\n10512|| <code>created_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp or null |\n10513|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10514|\n10515|<code>Actor</code> contains exactly <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10516|<code>kind:main|subagent|external</code>,\n10517|<code>parent_actor_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>name:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10518|<code>source_native_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10519|<code>model:string[1..512]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Exactly one\n10520|actor is <code>main</code>; only it has null parent.\n10521|\n10522|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n10523|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>event_id</code>,\n10524|<code>logical_session_id</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n10525|<code>parents:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>, <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10526|<code>turn_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>kind</code>,\n10527|<code>timestamp:timestamp|null</code>,\n10528|<code>visibility:public|projection|internal|opaque</code>,\n10529|<code>payload</code>, <code>source_evidence</code>, and\n10530|<code>extensions</code>. Schema/version are exact canonical-event 1.0.0 and\n10531|event ID is the JCS digest with only itself omitted. Ordinals are contiguous\n10532|from zero.\n10533|\n10534|<code>SourceEvidence</code> contains exactly\n10535|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10536|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10537|<code>native_event_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10538|<code>native_type:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10539|<code>raw_refs:sorted unique RawReference[0..65536]</code>,\n10540|<code>capture_status:exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code>,\n10541|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10542|<code>core_operation_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10543|<code>RawReference</code> contains exactly <code>manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10544|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>, and\n10545|<code>length:uint53</code>. Synthesized requires null native Event ID and a\n10546|non-null core operation; all other statuses require null core operation.\n10547|\n10548|#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\n10549|\n10550|The dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\n10551|Every non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\n10552|<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\n10553|or a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\n10554|Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\n10555|raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\n10556|item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\n10557|1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\n10558|by kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\n10559|native resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\n10560|replace item gates.\n10561|\n10562|Profiles are <code>strict_exact|maximal_safe|compact|messages_only|archive_only</code>;\n10563|maximal-safe is default. Strategies are\n10564|<code>same_environment_native_rewrite|target_native_writer|target_official_import|continuation_context|archive_only</code>.\n10565|Continuation context is explicitly non-native historical fidelity.\n10566|\n10567|Projection Plan 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, Capture/Canonical inputs,\n10568|source/target tuples, expected new native ID, strategy/profile, ordered\n10569|item mappings and reasons, target operations/resources, exclusions, limits,\n10570|<code>fidelity_basis_digest</code>, and extensions. It never predicts a final\n10571|Fidelity Report ID. Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 binds plan and target\n10572|ID to sorted disjoint blob/directory entries partitioned by operation sequence.\n10573|It grants no live authority and cannot populate a Checkpoint.\n10574|\n10575|Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 binds operation,\n10576|<code>staged|live</code>, plan/projected manifest, equal expected/observed\n10577|native IDs, target tuple, parsed count/heads, Workspace Binding, structural\n10578|digest, and sorted evidence blobs. Modes cannot be relabeled. Clone Validation\n10579|Report 1.0.0 aggregates both reads, identity/workspace/marker/resume checks,\n10580|Fidelity Report, findings, and valid result; every applicable check must pass.\n10581|\n10582|Migration Checkpoint 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, source snapshot and optional\n10583|AX Checkpoint, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, tuples, previous checkpoint/\n10584|receipt, policy and fidelity-basis hashes, visible low-authority projection,\n10585|and extensions. It does not name the final report. Visible text comes from\n10586|typed escaped fields and is user context, never an assistant reply or control\n10587|instruction.\n10588|\n10589|Clone Lineage Receipt 1.0.0 binds source/target identities and tuples,\n10590|Migration Checkpoint, Projection Plan, G3, final reports, Provider commit fact,\n10591|target Checkpoint, committed event, and optional prior receipt. It names G3,\n10592|never G4; G4 names it. Lineage is descriptive, never authorization.\n10593|\n10594|The following are the complete closed schemas for those contracts.\n10595|\n10596|<code>FidelityCounts</code> contains exactly the seven uint53 members\n10597|<code>exact</code>, <code>semantic</code>, <code>summarized</code>,\n10598|<code>opaque_preserved</code>, <code>synthesized</code>, <code>omitted</code>,\n10599|and <code>unrecoverable</code>.\n10600|\n10601|<code>FidelityDispositionRecord</code> contains exactly\n10602|<code>source_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10603|<code>source_class:string[1..128]</code>,\n10604|<code>source_evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..65536]</code>,\n10605|<code>canonical_object_id:digest|null</code>,\n10606|<code>target_locator:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10607|<code>disposition:exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>,\n10608|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10609|<code>explanation:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10610|<code>staged_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>,\n10611|<code>live_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>, and\n10612|<code>extensions</code>. Exact requires an empty reason set; every other\n10613|disposition requires at least one reason. Synthesized requires no source\n10614|canonical object; every non-synthesized row traces to captured source evidence.\n10615|\n10616|Fidelity Report 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10617|\n10618|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10619|| --- | --- |\n10620|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:fidelity-report</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10621|| <code>fidelity_report_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10622|| <code>scope</code> | <code>archive&#124;target</code> |\n10623|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 operation / bundle chain |\n10624|| <code>source_snapshot_digest</code> | Terminal captured snapshot digest |\n10625|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> / <code>canonical_session_id</code> | Exact lower immutable inputs |\n10626|| <code>projection_plan_id</code> | digest or null; null exactly for archive |\n10627|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact source tuple |\n10628|| <code>target_environment</code> | Exact target tuple or null; null exactly for archive |\n10629|| <code>profile</code> | Closed fidelity profile; <code>archive_only</code> exactly for archive |\n10630|| <code>required_dispositions</code> | Closed map from class to sorted unique non-empty disposition sets |\n10631|| <code>forbid_reasons</code> | Sorted unique string[1..128][0..128] |\n10632|| <code>dispositions</code> | <code>FidelityDispositionRecord[1..1000000]</code>, sorted unique by source item key with synthesized rows ordered after source rows |\n10633|| <code>counts</code> | Exact <code>FidelityCounts</code>, derived from disposition rows |\n10634|| <code>event_kind_counts</code> | Closed map of every Canonical Event kind to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10635|| <code>content_block_counts</code> | Closed map of every content-block type to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10636|| <code>byte_counts</code> | Closed map of every disposition to uint53 |\n10637|| <code>reason_counts</code> | Sorted map string[1..128] to uint53&gt;0 |\n10638|| <code>raw_bundle_complete</code> / <code>canonical_complete</code> | Core-derived booleans |\n10639|| <code>target_semantically_continuable</code> / <code>target_natively_resumable</code> | Core-derived booleans; both false for archive |\n10640|| <code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> / <code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> | digest or null; both null for archive and both non-null for target |\n10641|| <code>adapter_attestations</code> | Sorted unique digest[0..64], evidence only |\n10642|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10643|\n10644|Every Capture Manifest item and Canonical Event occurs in exactly one\n10645|non-synthesized disposition row. Aggregate maps reconcile exactly to the rows\n10646|and cannot replace them. A target report does not name Clone Validation Report,\n10647|Lineage Receipt, G4, or a future event. An archive report references only the\n10648|G0/G1 closure and is therefore targetless.\n10649|\n10650|Projection Plan 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10651|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6cd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":449,"recorded_at":1780531400000893,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96"},"task_id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b329-c314-71f3-a2fb-fbe1cdb48e96"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":450,"recorded_at":1780531400000895,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b329bf8474319fde58d790e4b4c0","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(10321 line(s) above)\n10322|### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\n10323|\n10324|A clone is a derivation, never a move or fork alias. It MUST leave source\n10325|bytes, Session Record, provider ID, lease, workspace authority, task-board\n10326|binding, and native identity unchanged. It creates one new direct Session\n10327|Record 2.0.0, target workspace identity, native identity, and epoch-1 lease.\n10328|The target accepts no input until transaction, target Checkpoint, lineage, and\n10329|optional ordinary resume validation succeed.\n10330|\n10331|#### 13.14.1 Capture and canonical contracts\n10332|\n10333|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains its\n10334|schema/version/omission-rule ID, operation ID, source Environment Tuple, and\n10335|sorted unique entries. Each entry has sanitized native\n10336|key, capture class, byte count, blob ID, Blob Descriptor ID, and extensions.\n10337|It contains no credential, runtime, lock, target, AX lease, or fabricated AX\n10338|Session/Provider identity.\n10339|\n10340|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version/ID,\n10341|operation/bundle, source basis, source Environment Tuple, sanitized Native\n10342|Identity, capture-plan digest, Capture Boundary, Raw Object Manifest ID,\n10343|sorted Capture Items, exact excluded classes, core-derived\n10344|<code>raw_complete</code>, creator/time, and extensions. Source basis is\n10345|<code>ax_session</code> with source Session/Record/Checkpoint/Provider Identity\n10346|IDs or <code>external_native</code> with a sanitized source reference.\n10347|\n10348|Each Capture Item has one native key and class\n10349|<code>durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>.\n10350|It is <code>included</code> with descriptor/count and no reason, or\n10351|<code>excluded</code> with null content fields and a stable reason. Credential,\n10352|auth, runtime, and lock classes are excluded. Unknown makes raw completeness\n10353|false and blocks maximal-safe.\n10354|\n10355|Capture Boundary is <code>stable</code> with Stable Snapshot Proof, or\n10356|<code>unstable_archive</code> with generation, pre/post digests,\n10357|<code>source_not_quiescent</code>, explicit acknowledgement, and\n10358|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>. Stable proof records\n10359|<code>closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10360|generation, optional immutable identity, equal pre/post digests, and\n10361|input/foreground/background idle facts. Size equality is never proof. The\n10362|unstable form is core-created only for archive-only output and cannot enter a\n10363|target branch.\n10364|\n10365|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10366|logical Session UUIDv7, source Environment Tuple/native ID, nullable title,\n10367|closed Workspace Binding, 1..1024 Actors, 1..1,000,000 ordered unique Event\n10368|IDs, 1..1024 head IDs, nullable source created/updated times, and extensions.\n10369|Actor contains exactly actor UUIDv7, <code>main|subagent|external</code>,\n10370|nullable parent (null only for main), nullable name/source-native ID/model, and\n10371|extensions.\n10372|\n10373|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10374|logical Session UUIDv7, zero-based contiguous ordinal, 0..64 sorted unique\n10375|causal parents, Actor UUIDv7, nullable turn UUIDv7, kind, nullable source time,\n10376|<code>public|projection|internal|opaque</code> visibility, kind-selected closed\n10377|payload, Source Evidence, and extensions. Source Evidence contains environment\n10378|and native Session IDs, nullable native Event ID/type, sorted unique raw\n10379|blob/manifest byte-range references,\n10380|<code>exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code> capture status, and stable\n10381|reason codes. Synthesized events have no native Event ID and identify the core\n10382|operation.\n10383|\n10384|The exact event kinds are\n10385|<code>session_started|instruction_snapshot|user_message|assistant_message|reasoning_summary|opaque_reasoning|tool_definition_snapshot|tool_call|tool_result|approval_request|approval_response|plan_update|progress|usage|rate_limit|file_change|compaction|turn_started|turn_completed|turn_aborted|subagent_started|subagent_completed|error|migration_checkpoint|session_finished|opaque_event</code>.\n10386|Payloads contain only their registered typed facts. Message-like payloads use\n10387|exactly <code>text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque</code>\n10388|content blocks with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references; inline\n10389|content is at most 64 KiB. Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque\n10390|events. Historical tools\n10391|are inert; incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action.\n10392|Foreign instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\n10393|reasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target accounting.\n10394|\n10395|The following closed shapes govern this subsection; the preceding prose is a\n10396|summary and does not permit omitted or additional members.\n10397|\n10398|<code>NativeIdentity</code> contains exactly\n10399|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10400|<code>identity_kind:provider_native|official_import|continuation_context</code>,\n10401|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10402|<code>backend_realm_fingerprint:digest|null</code>,\n10403|<code>opaque_identity:string[1..512]|null</code>, and\n10404|<code>extensions</code>. It contains no credential, absolute source path as\n10405|cross-host identity, PID, socket, token, or secret environment value.\n10406|\n10407|<code>WorkspaceBinding</code> contains exactly\n10408|<code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10409|<code>cwd_relative:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10410|<code>repository_remote_fingerprints:sorted unique digest[0..128]</code>,\n10411|<code>branch:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10412|<code>head_digest:digest|null</code>, <code>index_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10413|<code>working_tree_digest:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10414|The relative cwd is normalized beneath the Workspace Group root; no member\n10415|grants filesystem authority.\n10416|\n10417|Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10418|\n10419|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10420|| --- | --- |\n10421|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-raw-object-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10422|| <code>raw_object_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10423|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation |\n10424|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact probed <code>EnvironmentTuple</code> |\n10425|| <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Sanitized string[1..512], never an AX Session ID |\n10426|| <code>source_identity_digest</code> | Terminal digest of canonical sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> bytes |\n10427|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Exact core-validated capture-plan digest |\n10428|| <code>entries</code> | <code>RawObjectEntry[0..65536]</code>, sorted unique by native item key |\n10429|| <code>total_bytes</code> | uint53 equal to the sum of entry byte counts |\n10430|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys with no normative reference |\n10431|\n10432|<code>RawObjectEntry</code> contains exactly\n10433|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10434|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|unknown</code>,\n10435|<code>byte_count:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, and\n10436|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>. The descriptor agrees with blob ID and\n10437|byte count. Credential, machine-auth, runtime-state, transient-lock, and\n10438|excluded candidates are forbidden.\n10439|\n10440|Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10441|\n10442|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10443|| --- | --- |\n10444|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:clone-capture-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10445|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10446|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 clone operation / logical bundle chain |\n10447|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Capture Source Basis below |\n10448|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_identity</code> | Exact tuple / sanitized <code>NativeIdentity</code> |\n10449|| <code>capture_plan_digest</code> | Terminal digest of the complete canonical capture-plan success body |\n10450|| <code>capture_boundary</code> | Closed Capture Boundary below |\n10451|| <code>source_raw_object_manifest_id</code> | Exact raw manifest containing all and only included objects |\n10452|| <code>items</code> | <code>CaptureItem[0..65536]</code>, sorted bytewise by native item key; one per plan candidate |\n10453|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | Sorted unique capture-class[0..9], exactly the excluded-row classes |\n10454|| <code>raw_complete</code> | Core-derived boolean; true only after complete plan/object reconciliation |\n10455|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> / <code>created_at</code> | UUIDv7 / diagnostic timestamp |\n10456|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10457|\n10458|Capture Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_session</code> contains\n10459|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10460|<code>source_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n10461|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10462|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, and\n10463|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=external_native</code> contains exactly\n10464|<code>kind</code>, <code>external_source_ref:string[1..512]</code>, and\n10465|<code>extensions</code>.\n10466|\n10467|<code>CaptureItem</code> contains exactly\n10468|<code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10469|<code>class:durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown</code>,\n10470|<code>disposition:included|excluded</code>,\n10471|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest|null</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n10472|<code>exclusion_reason:string[1..128]|null</code>, and\n10473|<code>extensions</code>. Included requires both content members non-null and a\n10474|null reason. Excluded requires null content members and a non-null reason.\n10475|Credential, auth, runtime, and lock classes are always excluded. Unknown makes\n10476|<code>raw_complete=false</code> and blocks <code>maximal_safe</code>.\n10477|\n10478|Capture Boundary is a closed union. <code>kind=stable</code> contains exactly\n10479|<code>kind</code>, <code>proof:StableSnapshotProof</code>, and\n10480|<code>extensions</code>. <code>kind=unstable_archive</code> contains exactly\n10481|<code>kind</code>, <code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10482|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10483|<code>reason_code=source_not_quiescent</code>,\n10484|<code>operator_explicit=true</code>,\n10485|<code>target_projection_forbidden=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10486|Only core may construct the unstable archive form; G2 always rejects it.\n10487|\n10488|<code>StableSnapshotProof</code> contains exactly\n10489|<code>proof_kind:closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence</code>,\n10490|<code>source_generation:string[1..512]</code>,\n10491|<code>snapshot_identity_digest:digest|null</code>,\n10492|<code>pre_capture_digest:digest</code>, <code>post_capture_digest:digest</code>,\n10493|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n10494|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Capture\n10495|digests are equal. Closed-store/provider-quiescence requires all booleans true\n10496|and null snapshot identity; immutable-snapshot/log-prefix requires non-null\n10497|identity. File-size equality is never proof.\n10498|\n10499|Canonical Session 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10500|\n10501|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10502|| --- | --- |\n10503|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:canonical-session</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10504|| <code>canonical_session_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10505|| <code>logical_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 stable within bundle lineage |\n10506|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>source_native_session_id</code> | Exact tuple / string[1..512] |\n10507|| <code>title</code> | string[1..4096] or null |\n10508|| <code>workspace</code> | Closed <code>WorkspaceBinding</code> |\n10509|| <code>actors</code> | <code>Actor[1..1024]</code>, unique by actor ID |\n10510|| <code>event_ids</code> | Ordered unique digest[1..1000000] |\n10511|| <code>head_event_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[1..1024], all in event IDs |\n10512|| <code>created_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp or null |\n10513|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10514|\n10515|<code>Actor</code> contains exactly <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10516|<code>kind:main|subagent|external</code>,\n10517|<code>parent_actor_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>name:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10518|<code>source_native_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10519|<code>model:string[1..512]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Exactly one\n10520|actor is <code>main</code>; only it has null parent.\n10521|\n10522|Canonical Event 1.0.0 contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n10523|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>event_id</code>,\n10524|<code>logical_session_id</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n10525|<code>parents:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>, <code>actor_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10526|<code>turn_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, <code>kind</code>,\n10527|<code>timestamp:timestamp|null</code>,\n10528|<code>visibility:public|projection|internal|opaque</code>,\n10529|<code>payload</code>, <code>source_evidence</code>, and\n10530|<code>extensions</code>. Schema/version are exact canonical-event 1.0.0 and\n10531|event ID is the JCS digest with only itself omitted. Ordinals are contiguous\n10532|from zero.\n10533|\n10534|<code>SourceEvidence</code> contains exactly\n10535|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10536|<code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10537|<code>native_event_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10538|<code>native_type:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n10539|<code>raw_refs:sorted unique RawReference[0..65536]</code>,\n10540|<code>capture_status:exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable</code>,\n10541|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10542|<code>core_operation_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10543|<code>RawReference</code> contains exactly <code>manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10544|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>, and\n10545|<code>length:uint53</code>. Synthesized requires null native Event ID and a\n10546|non-null core operation; all other statuses require null core operation.\n10547|\n10548|#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\n10549|\n10550|The dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\n10551|Every non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\n10552|<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\n10553|or a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\n10554|Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\n10555|raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\n10556|item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\n10557|1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\n10558|by kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\n10559|native resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\n10560|replace item gates.\n10561|\n10562|Profiles are <code>strict_exact|maximal_safe|compact|messages_only|archive_only</code>;\n10563|maximal-safe is default. Strategies are\n10564|<code>same_environment_native_rewrite|target_native_writer|target_official_import|continuation_context|archive_only</code>.\n10565|Continuation context is explicitly non-native historical fidelity.\n10566|\n10567|Projection Plan 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, Capture/Canonical inputs,\n10568|source/target tuples, expected new native ID, strategy/profile, ordered\n10569|item mappings and reasons, target operations/resources, exclusions, limits,\n10570|<code>fidelity_basis_digest</code>, and extensions. It never predicts a final\n10571|Fidelity Report ID. Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 binds plan and target\n10572|ID to sorted disjoint blob/directory entries partitioned by operation sequence.\n10573|It grants no live authority and cannot populate a Checkpoint.\n10574|\n10575|Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 binds operation,\n10576|<code>staged|live</code>, plan/projected manifest, equal expected/observed\n10577|native IDs, target tuple, parsed count/heads, Workspace Binding, structural\n10578|digest, and sorted evidence blobs. Modes cannot be relabeled. Clone Validation\n10579|Report 1.0.0 aggregates both reads, identity/workspace/marker/resume checks,\n10580|Fidelity Report, findings, and valid result; every applicable check must pass.\n10581|\n10582|Migration Checkpoint 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, source snapshot and optional\n10583|AX Checkpoint, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, tuples, previous checkpoint/\n10584|receipt, policy and fidelity-basis hashes, visible low-authority projection,\n10585|and extensions. It does not name the final report. Visible text comes from\n10586|typed escaped fields and is user context, never an assistant reply or control\n10587|instruction.\n10588|\n10589|Clone Lineage Receipt 1.0.0 binds source/target identities and tuples,\n10590|Migration Checkpoint, Projection Plan, G3, final reports, Provider commit fact,\n10591|target Checkpoint, committed event, and optional prior receipt. It names G3,\n10592|never G4; G4 names it. Lineage is descriptive, never authorization.\n10593|\n10594|The following are the complete closed schemas for those contracts.\n10595|\n10596|<code>FidelityCounts</code> contains exactly the seven uint53 members\n10597|<code>exact</code>, <code>semantic</code>, <code>summarized</code>,\n10598|<code>opaque_preserved</code>, <code>synthesized</code>, <code>omitted</code>,\n10599|and <code>unrecoverable</code>.\n10600|\n10601|<code>FidelityDispositionRecord</code> contains exactly\n10602|<code>source_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10603|<code>source_class:string[1..128]</code>,\n10604|<code>source_evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..65536]</code>,\n10605|<code>canonical_object_id:digest|null</code>,\n10606|<code>target_locator:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10607|<code>disposition:exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>,\n10608|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10609|<code>explanation:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10610|<code>staged_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>,\n10611|<code>live_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>, and\n10612|<code>extensions</code>. Exact requires an empty reason set; every other\n10613|disposition requires at least one reason. Synthesized requires no source\n10614|canonical object; every non-synthesized row traces to captured source evidence.\n10615|\n10616|Fidelity Report 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10617|\n10618|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10619|| --- | --- |\n10620|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:fidelity-report</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10621|| <code>fidelity_report_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10622|| <code>scope</code> | <code>archive&#124;target</code> |\n10623|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 operation / bundle chain |\n10624|| <code>source_snapshot_digest</code> | Terminal captured snapshot digest |\n10625|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> / <code>canonical_session_id</code> | Exact lower immutable inputs |\n10626|| <code>projection_plan_id</code> | digest or null; null exactly for archive |\n10627|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact source tuple |\n10628|| <code>target_environment</code> | Exact target tuple or null; null exactly for archive |\n10629|| <code>profile</code> | Closed fidelity profile; <code>archive_only</code> exactly for archive |\n10630|| <code>required_dispositions</code> | Closed map from class to sorted unique non-empty disposition sets |\n10631|| <code>forbid_reasons</code> | Sorted unique string[1..128][0..128] |\n10632|| <code>dispositions</code> | <code>FidelityDispositionRecord[1..1000000]</code>, sorted unique by source item key with synthesized rows ordered after source rows |\n10633|| <code>counts</code> | Exact <code>FidelityCounts</code>, derived from disposition rows |\n10634|| <code>event_kind_counts</code> | Closed map of every Canonical Event kind to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10635|| <code>content_block_counts</code> | Closed map of every content-block type to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10636|| <code>byte_counts</code> | Closed map of every disposition to uint53 |\n10637|| <code>reason_counts</code> | Sorted map string[1..128] to uint53&gt;0 |\n10638|| <code>raw_bundle_complete</code> / <code>canonical_complete</code> | Core-derived booleans |\n10639|| <code>target_semantically_continuable</code> / <code>target_natively_resumable</code> | Core-derived booleans; both false for archive |\n10640|| <code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> / <code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> | digest or null; both null for archive and both non-null for target |\n10641|| <code>adapter_attestations</code> | Sorted unique digest[0..64], evidence only |\n10642|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10643|\n10644|Every Capture Manifest item and Canonical Event occurs in exactly one\n10645|non-synthesized disposition row. Aggregate maps reconcile exactly to the rows\n10646|and cannot replace them. A target report does not name Clone Validation Report,\n10647|Lineage Receipt, G4, or a future event. An archive report references only the\n10648|G0/G1 closure and is therefore targetless.\n10649|\n10650|Projection Plan 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10651|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
