{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c701","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":475,"recorded_at":1780531400000945,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3"},"task_id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(3737 line(s) above)\n3738|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3739|\n3740|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3741|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3742|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3743|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3744|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3745|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3746|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3747|\n3748|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3749|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3750|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3751|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3752|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3753|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3754|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3755|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3756|\n3757|The closed operation registry is:\n3758|\n3759|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3760|| --- | --- |\n3761|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3762|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3763|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3764|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3765|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3766|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3767|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3768|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3769|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3770|\n3771|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3772|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3773|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3774|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3775|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3776|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3777|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3778|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3779|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3780|every candidate object.\n3781|\n3782|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3783|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3784|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3785|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3786|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3787|\n3788|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3789|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3790|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3791|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3792|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3793|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3794|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3795|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3796|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3797|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3798|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3799|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3800|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3801|  never paths.\n3802|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3803|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3804|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3805|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3806|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3807|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3808|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3809|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3810|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3811|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3812|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3813|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3814|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3815|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3816|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3817|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3818|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3819|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3820|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3821|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3822|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3823|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3824|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3825|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3826|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3827|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3828|\n3829|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3830|\n3831|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3832|| --- | --- | --- |\n3833|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3834|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3835|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3836|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3837|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3838|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3839|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3840|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3841|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3842|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3843|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3844|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3845|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3846|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3847|\n3848|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3849|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3850|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3851|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3852|and never fallback permission.\n3853|\n3854|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3855|\n3856|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3857|| --- | --- |\n3858|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3859|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3860|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3861|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3862|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3863|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3864|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3865|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3866|\n3867|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c703","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":476,"recorded_at":1780531400000947,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3"},"task_id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b329-d136-72f2-8002-03ce19a959d3"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c705","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":477,"recorded_at":1780531400000949,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74"},"task_id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(4850 line(s) above)\n4851|### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\n4852|\n4853|A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata\n4854|MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that\n4855|references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,\n4856|and atomically install it in the object store.\n4857|\n4858|Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and\n4859|metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.\n4860|\n4861|Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema\n4862|<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be\n4863|sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly\n4864|<code>size</code> bytes:\n4865|\n4866|The descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4867|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4868|<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,\n4869|<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and\n4870|<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase\n4871|ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and\n4872|contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,\n4873|<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes\n4874|start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;\n4875|a non-empty blob has at least one.\n4876|\n4877|~~~json\n4878|{\n4879|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n4880|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4881|  \"descriptor_id\": \"sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee\",\n4882|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4883|  \"size\": 11,\n4884|  \"media_type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n4885|  \"chunks\": [\n4886|    {\n4887|      \"index\": 0,\n4888|      \"offset\": 0,\n4889|      \"size\": 11,\n4890|      \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4891|    }\n4892|  ]\n4893|}\n4894|~~~\n4895|\n4896|The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with\n4897|<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes\n4898|<code>ax-example\\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is\n4899|<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the\n4900|whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits\n4901|at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.\n4902|A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before\n4903|publishing a partial manifest.\n4904|\n4905|### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\n4906|\n4907|The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is\n4908|<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n4909|\n4910|The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4911|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4912|<code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>index:uint32</code>,\n4913|<code>offset:uint53</code>, <code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n4914|<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index\n4915|times 4,194,304; every non-final chunk has that exact size.\n4916|\n4917|~~~json\n4918|{\n4919|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:chunk\",\n4920|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4921|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4922|  \"index\": 0,\n4923|  \"offset\": 0,\n4924|  \"size\": 11,\n4925|  \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4926|}\n4927|~~~\n4928|\n4929|Chunk digests are over raw chunk bytes. A receiver MUST validate every chunk\n4930|before marking it present and MUST validate the complete blob after assembly.\n4931|Chunk identity is transfer metadata; the whole blob digest is storage identity.\n4932|\n4933|### 10.4 Transfer Manifest\n4934|\n4935|Transfer Manifest schema <code>urn:ax:schema:transfer-manifest</code> version\n4936|<code>1.0.0</code> describes one immutable snapshot. Its top-level object is\n4937|closed and contains exactly:\n4938|\n4939|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n4940|| --- | --- | --- |\n4941|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Transfer Manifest schema identifier |\n4942|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n4943|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n4944|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace_group</code>, <code>workspace_tree</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n4945|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Group, workspace, or session selected by kind |\n4946|| <code>base_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for an initial capture with no predecessor checkpoint |\n4947|| <code>entries</code> | ManifestEntry[0..65536] | Sorted bytewise by normalized path |\n4948|| <code>child_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Path-disjoint child/partition closure |\n4949|| <code>workspace_snapshot</code> | WorkspaceSnapshot or null | Non-null only for <code>workspace_group</code> |\n4950|| <code>provider_identity_record_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>provider</code> |\n4951|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>task_board</code> |\n4952|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | sorted unique string[0..128] | Applied exclusion-policy classes |\n4953|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Capturing host |\n4954|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n4955|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n4956|\n4957|The kind invariants are exact:\n4958|\n4959|- <code>workspace_group</code> uses the Workspace Group ID as subject, requires\n4960|  a non-null workspace snapshot and at least one child, and requires empty\n4961|  entries plus null provider/task-board IDs;\n4962|- <code>workspace_tree</code> uses one Workspace ID as subject, requires null\n4963|  snapshot/provider/task-board fields, and contains entries and optional\n4964|  path-partition children;\n4965|- <code>provider</code> uses a Session ID, requires a provider identity record,\n4966|  and requires null snapshot/task-board fields;\n4967|- <code>task_board</code> uses a Session ID, requires a bundle ID, and requires\n4968|  null snapshot/provider fields; and\n4969|- <code>composite</code> requires at least one child, empty entries, and all\n4970|  three tagged fields null.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c707","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":478,"recorded_at":1780531400000951,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74"},"task_id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b329-d157-7340-91b6-d53c10809e74"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c709","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":479,"recorded_at":1780531400000953,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b329caf2764b80b663934fab2710","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(3737 line(s) above)\n3738|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3739|\n3740|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3741|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3742|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3743|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3744|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3745|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3746|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3747|\n3748|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3749|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3750|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3751|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3752|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3753|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3754|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3755|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3756|\n3757|The closed operation registry is:\n3758|\n3759|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3760|| --- | --- |\n3761|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3762|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3763|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3764|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3765|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3766|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3767|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3768|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3769|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3770|\n3771|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3772|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3773|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3774|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3775|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3776|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3777|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3778|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3779|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3780|every candidate object.\n3781|\n3782|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3783|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3784|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3785|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3786|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3787|\n3788|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3789|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3790|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3791|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3792|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3793|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3794|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3795|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3796|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3797|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3798|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3799|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3800|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3801|  never paths.\n3802|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3803|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3804|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3805|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3806|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3807|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3808|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3809|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3810|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3811|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3812|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3813|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3814|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3815|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3816|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3817|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3818|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3819|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3820|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3821|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3822|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3823|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3824|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3825|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3826|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3827|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3828|\n3829|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3830|\n3831|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3832|| --- | --- | --- |\n3833|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3834|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3835|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3836|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3837|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3838|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3839|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3840|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3841|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3842|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3843|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3844|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3845|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3846|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3847|\n3848|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3849|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3850|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3851|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3852|and never fallback permission.\n3853|\n3854|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3855|\n3856|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3857|| --- | --- |\n3858|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3859|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3860|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3861|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3862|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3863|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3864|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3865|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3866|\n3867|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c70b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":480,"recorded_at":1780531400000955,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b329cd9272e4b694177a5dfe972c","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(4850 line(s) above)\n4851|### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\n4852|\n4853|A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata\n4854|MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that\n4855|references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,\n4856|and atomically install it in the object store.\n4857|\n4858|Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and\n4859|metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.\n4860|\n4861|Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema\n4862|<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be\n4863|sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly\n4864|<code>size</code> bytes:\n4865|\n4866|The descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4867|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4868|<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,\n4869|<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and\n4870|<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase\n4871|ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and\n4872|contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,\n4873|<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes\n4874|start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;\n4875|a non-empty blob has at least one.\n4876|\n4877|~~~json\n4878|{\n4879|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n4880|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4881|  \"descriptor_id\": \"sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee\",\n4882|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4883|  \"size\": 11,\n4884|  \"media_type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n4885|  \"chunks\": [\n4886|    {\n4887|      \"index\": 0,\n4888|      \"offset\": 0,\n4889|      \"size\": 11,\n4890|      \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4891|    }\n4892|  ]\n4893|}\n4894|~~~\n4895|\n4896|The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with\n4897|<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes\n4898|<code>ax-example\\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is\n4899|<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the\n4900|whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits\n4901|at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.\n4902|A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before\n4903|publishing a partial manifest.\n4904|\n4905|### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\n4906|\n4907|The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is\n4908|<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n4909|\n4910|The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4911|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4912|<code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>index:uint32</code>,\n4913|<code>offset:uint53</code>, <code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n4914|<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index\n4915|times 4,194,304; every non-final chunk has that exact size.\n4916|\n4917|~~~json\n4918|{\n4919|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:chunk\",\n4920|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4921|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4922|  \"index\": 0,\n4923|  \"offset\": 0,\n4924|  \"size\": 11,\n4925|  \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4926|}\n4927|~~~\n4928|\n4929|Chunk digests are over raw chunk bytes. A receiver MUST validate every chunk\n4930|before marking it present and MUST validate the complete blob after assembly.\n4931|Chunk identity is transfer metadata; the whole blob digest is storage identity.\n4932|\n4933|### 10.4 Transfer Manifest\n4934|\n4935|Transfer Manifest schema <code>urn:ax:schema:transfer-manifest</code> version\n4936|<code>1.0.0</code> describes one immutable snapshot. Its top-level object is\n4937|closed and contains exactly:\n4938|\n4939|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n4940|| --- | --- | --- |\n4941|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Transfer Manifest schema identifier |\n4942|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n4943|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n4944|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace_group</code>, <code>workspace_tree</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n4945|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Group, workspace, or session selected by kind |\n4946|| <code>base_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for an initial capture with no predecessor checkpoint |\n4947|| <code>entries</code> | ManifestEntry[0..65536] | Sorted bytewise by normalized path |\n4948|| <code>child_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Path-disjoint child/partition closure |\n4949|| <code>workspace_snapshot</code> | WorkspaceSnapshot or null | Non-null only for <code>workspace_group</code> |\n4950|| <code>provider_identity_record_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>provider</code> |\n4951|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>task_board</code> |\n4952|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | sorted unique string[0..128] | Applied exclusion-policy classes |\n4953|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Capturing host |\n4954|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n4955|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n4956|\n4957|The kind invariants are exact:\n4958|\n4959|- <code>workspace_group</code> uses the Workspace Group ID as subject, requires\n4960|  a non-null workspace snapshot and at least one child, and requires empty\n4961|  entries plus null provider/task-board IDs;\n4962|- <code>workspace_tree</code> uses one Workspace ID as subject, requires null\n4963|  snapshot/provider/task-board fields, and contains entries and optional\n4964|  path-partition children;\n4965|- <code>provider</code> uses a Session ID, requires a provider identity record,\n4966|  and requires null snapshot/task-board fields;\n4967|- <code>task_board</code> uses a Session ID, requires a bundle ID, and requires\n4968|  null snapshot/provider fields; and\n4969|- <code>composite</code> requires at least one child, empty entries, and all\n4970|  three tagged fields null.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
