task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the ordering mutants prove the gate precedes the seal at both entries: `N-race-order-capture` (manifest scan), `N-race-order-project` (seal error message), `N-race-order-project-seal` (capture-store scan at the projection entry). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, excluded size change, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 41 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260918-fdce92; no base move, still `2f844bb` over trunk `a12d1bd`; `origin/main` still `c3aae73`): row 8 sealed unstable pre/post digests + generation asserted against the measurements (`N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post`); row 10 capture-store manifest scan at `CaptureAndProject` (`N-race-order-project-seal`, killed by the scan — `N-race-order-project` is killed by the seal error message); P3-a unplanned-symlink row, P3-b symlinked-store-root row, P3-c excluded-size row (shipped, not rew