{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd61","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":1291,"recorded_at":1780531400002577,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3309d22731ca1be46dd2cfc5620","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-42-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"func expectedSectionBindingInventory\\\" -A 30 internal/traceability/traceability.go | head -40; echo ===; sed -n '3895,3920p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check binding inventory and 7.8 clause 2\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"729:func expectedSectionBindingInventory() map[string]struct{} {\\n730-\\tresult := make(map[string]struct{})\\n731-\\tfor _, identifier := range specpin.SectionInventoryV070() {\\n732-\\t\\tresult[sectionBindingKey(identifier)] = struct{}{}\\n733-\\t}\\n734-\\treturn result\\n735-}\\n736-\\n737-func expectedCatalogSectionBindings(value catalog.Catalog) (map[string]struct{}, error) {\\n738-\\tresult := make(map[string]struct{})\\n739-\\taddDefinition := func(normativeSection string, fixtures []string) error {\\n740-\\t\\tfor _, expression := range strings.Split(normativeSection, \\\",\\\") {\\n741-\\t\\t\\texpression = strings.TrimSpace(expression)\\n742-\\t\\t\\tparts := strings.Split(expression, \\\"-\\\")\\n743-\\t\\t\\tif len(parts) > 2 || len(parts) == 0 {\\n744-\\t\\t\\t\\treturn fail(\\\"catalog normative section %q is not an exact section or range\\\", normativeSection)\\n745-\\t\\t\\t}\\n746-\\t\\t\\tstart := canonicalNumericSection(strings.TrimSpace(parts[0]))\\n747-\\t\\t\\tend := start\\n748-\\t\\t\\tif len(parts) == 2 {\\n749-\\t\\t\\t\\tend = canonicalNumericSection(strings.TrimSpace(parts[1]))\\n750-\\t\\t\\t}\\n751-\\t\\t\\tidentifiers, err := expandV070SectionRange(start, end)\\n752-\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n753-\\t\\t\\t\\treturn fail(\\\"catalog normative section %q: %v\\\", normativeSection, err)\\n754-\\t\\t\\t}\\n755-\\t\\t\\tfor _, identifier := range identifiers {\\n756-\\t\\t\\t\\tresult[sectionBindingKey(identifier)] = struct{}{}\\n757-\\t\\t\\t}\\n758-\\t\\t}\\n759-\\t\\tfor _, fixture := range fixtures {\\n===\\nEach capability value contains exactly\\n<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\\n<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\\n<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\\nand <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\\nor contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\\n\\nFor source and target, the host seals a closed\\n<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\\n<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\\n<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\\n<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\\n<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\\n<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\\n<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\\n<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\\n<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\\ntarget mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\\nand the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\\nself-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\\n\\nA target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\\nnative-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\\nportable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\\naccepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\\nplus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2832,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 708,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
