s no binary or projection to\n3235|produce; Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n3236|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n3237|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; Section\n3238|5.3 at 7/8, bound to\n3239|[`internal/sessrepo`](internal/sessrepo), whose undischarged clause `5.3#5`\n3240|is the initiator-union maximum no takeover flow computes yet; Section\n3241|15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n3242|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n3243|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n3244|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n3245|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no\n3246|provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a TerminalBackend\n3247|capability. Structural RPC hello frames are built by\n3248|[`internal/rpcwire`](internal/rpcwire), which rejects an error map key, and\n3249|consumed by the authenticated [`internal/hostchannel`](internal/hostchannel)\n3250|handshake, which frames failures only as Error envelopes and never as hello\n3251|keys; neither clause is enumerated against an acceptance case, so both stay\n3252|undischarged. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n3253|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n3254|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n3255|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds and the clause\n3256|stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n3257|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n3258|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n3259|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n3260|requires every production refusal arm to be declared with a resolving named\n3261|asserting test in both directions; behavioral proof stays with each row's\n3262|named test, which the inventory resolves textually; and Section 7.7 at 3/4,\n3263|bound to [`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost), whose undischarged clause\n3264|`7.7#2` is the machine-local-alias sentence - the omit rule is enforced, but a\n3265|shell word that expands to unrestricted mode without spelling a table token is\n3266|beyond argv inspection),\n3267|four are\n3268|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n3269|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n3270|implementation; Section 5.5 at 1/3, whose discharged negative-battery clause\n3271|is enforced by identity creation and checking while the opaque-map content\n3272|rule stays half-decided; Section 8 at 4/12, whose discharged probe,\n3273|label-integrity, and row-separation clauses are enforced by the resume tuple\n3274|gate and the native-resume smoke while every materialization rule stays\n3275|unimplemented; and Section 2.2 at 4/22, bound to\n3276|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing), whose discharged clauses are the\n3277|single-owner, replica-restraint, winning-epoch-carriage, and\n3278|losing-event-rejection invariants while the replication, secret, store,\n3279|and directory invariants have no implementation), four are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.12, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n3280|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n3281|and fifty-two are `unevidenced`. Seven sections are recorded unowned.\n3282|All 13 sections added by v0.6.0 name pending task owners in the reviewed\n3283|registry gaps; these assignments grant no runtime admission. The\n3284|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md) separates\n3285|shared runtime APIs, their callers, product conformance and upstream source\n3286|publication validators, and preserves historical acceptance obligations.\n3287|The v0.7.0 revision adds no numbered section; its launch-plan, stdin,\n3288|caller_launch_plan, environment_drift and curator-run clause areas name\n3289|pending story owners in the reviewed registry gaps, and these assignments\n3290|grant no runtime admission either. The\n3291|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.7.0.md) attributes\n3292|each clause area to its implementing story and records the shared-section\n3293|splits.\n3294|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n3295|`-section 2.4` and nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its\n3296|ratio and its gap.\n3297|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n3298|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n3299|\n3300|Two admitted bindings out of sixty-eight cover five clauses, and that is\n3301|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n3302|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n3303|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n3304|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n3305|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n3306|Section 2.4 is the first multi-clause admission: its four clauses are\n3307|discharged by the `sessprofile-derive`, `sessprofile-derive-heads`,\n3308|`sessprofile-fork-pair`, and `provhost-mapping-resolution` acceptance cases.\n3309|\n3310|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n3311|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n3312|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n3313|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n3314|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n3315|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n3316|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n3317|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n3318|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n3319|`os.Exit` with it - the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` failure paths of\n3320|`cataloggen` and `tracecheck` - so clause `14.2#6` stays undischarged until an\n3321|`ax` binary exists; Section 7.3's closed Provider Manifest exists only as a catalog\n3322|row naming its URN; Section 6.5 requires the `required_capabilities` default to\n3323|be the platform lane minimum while `internal/config/validation.go` accepts only\n3324|an empty default; Section 17.2's single clause is an unknown-event reader\n3325|obligation while its binding now names the CLI Result machine reader `Read`,\n3326|which classifies one completed invocation rather than retaining any event, so it\n3327|does not discharge that clause either - an unknown error code and an inert\n3328|unknown extension are not an unknown session event, and the four numbered reader\n3329|rules that binding does implement carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are invisible to\n3330|the clause scanner; and Section 2.1's single clause is a replica runtime\n3331|obligation that no code here implements.\n3332|\n3333|The Session Adapter host surface lives in\n3334|[`internal/sessadapter`](internal/sessadapter): discovery binding\n3335|(`Discover`), manifest and probe decoding (`DecodeManifest`, `DecodeProbe`),\n3336|the closed fourteen-operation request/success bodies (`CheckRequestBody`,\n3337|`CheckSuccessBody`), resource limits (`DecodeResourceLimits`), the\n3338|request-digest binding and byte-for-byte context echo that carry this\n3339|package's idempotency (`VerifyRequestDigest`, `CheckContextEcho`, and the\n3340|fresh-sink rule), and the tuple-registry admission gates\n3341|(`CheckTupleAdmission`). Seven executable acceptance cases\n3342|(`session-adapter-discovery`, `session-adapter-manifest`,\n3343|`session-adapter-probe`, `session-adapter-operations`,\n3344|`session-adapter-limits`, `session-adapter-idempotency`,\n3345|`session-adapter-tuple-gates`) bind those entry points to their named\n3346|positive and refusal tests. The Section 7.8 clause-level binding stays\n3347|`unevidenced` (catalog `ForRelease` only): no clause of 7.8 is enumerated\n3348|against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim\n3349|about the obligations it carries.\n3350|\n3351|The Directory Node host surface lives in\n3352|[`internal/dirnode`](internal/dirnode): the two-major manifest\n3353|bootstrap (`DecideBootstrapStep` with its exact downgrade tuple,\n3354|`ProcessGuard`, `NextLowerMajor`), request/response envelope\n3355|framing (`EncodeRequest`, `DecodeRequestFrame`,\n3356|`CheckSuccessEnvelope`, `CheckFailureEnvelope`), manifest decoding\n3357|with façade binding checks (`DecodeManifest`,\n3358|`CheckManifestBindings`, `AvailableCapabilities`), per-major probe\n3359|framing with the node-build equality gate (`CheckProbeRequest`,\n3360|`CheckProbeResponse`, `CheckNodeBuildEqualsManifest`), scan\n3361|framing with the `(operation, operation_id)` idempotency journal\n3362|and its crash-recovery export/import (`CheckScanRequest`,\n3363|`CheckScanResponse`, `Journal`), and Session Directory Query\n3364|framing (`DecodeQuery`, `CheckCursorReuse`). Six executable\n3365|acceptance cases (`directory-node-bootstrap`,\n3366|`directory-node-manifest`, `directory-node-probe`,\n3367|`directory-node-scan`, `directory-node-query`,\n3368|`directory-node-idempotency`) bind those entry points to their\n3369|named positive and refusal tests, and an AST-derived refusal-arm\n3370|inventory (`census_test.go`) requires every production refusal arm\n3371|— literal, fault-detail conduit, and branch-prefix expression\n3372|shapes — to resolve to a named asserting test in both directions,\n3373|with two recorded defensive arms that no public input can fire.\n3374|The Section 7.9 clause-level binding stays `unevidenced` (catalog\n3375|`ForRelease` only): no clause of 7.9 is enumerated against an\n3376|acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim\n3377|about the obligations it carries. The framed subset is exactly\n3378|manifest, probe, and scan plus the Directory Query contract; the\n3379|remaining eight registry operations carry nested content owned by\n3380|the sibling leaves and are pinned as unframed by\n3381|`TestFramedSubsetIsExact`, not silently absent.\n3382|\n3383|Successful output reports ownership inventory counts and the measured coverage\n3384|ratio only. The gate does not mutate repository or product state, add an `ax`\n3385|command or `doctor` result, or claim that any catalog capability is available,\n3386|enabled, or supported.\n3387|\n3388|## Managed Skills\n3389|\n3390|`Skillfile.json` targets the Curator-standard `claude_code` and `codex_cli`\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
