{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e04f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":3714,"recorded_at":1780531400007423,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b349-a72d-7913-9da9-434933de5e1c"},"task_id":"01a0b349-a72d-7913-9da9-434933de5e1c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b349-a72d-7913-9da9-434933de5e1c","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-18\n-\n-### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\n+\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (matrix, invariants, 25-row refusal table, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure); 24 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite. No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n+- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` upgraded unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `9b9516d7…339e0b6` via the production marshal path); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=139, full=4, unevidenced=50, clauses 56/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` green; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, README figure pins); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\n+- INTEGRATION NOTE: this candidate is based on `a12d1bd` (trunk `c3aae73` not refreshed, per the no-move rule); trunk's mesh-RPC story added its own `storyUpgradedV070Bindings`/`storyNewV070Cases` entries and pin wants on top of the same base test. The orchestrator merge must union both stories' map entries and re-derive the pin (`cases=144`, `full=4`, `partial=8`, `sliver=5`, `unevidenced=47`, `clauses=63/569` expected — re-measure, do not copy).\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing; fact registries only for emitted kinds; framing-malformed lines refuse; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity, planning, lineage, transaction) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\n+\n+### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\n","final_result":true}}}
