{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f049","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b328-b328-7981-8beb-18f071df4b5f"},"sequence":5759,"recorded_at":1780531400011513,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8855960a-8895-4077-a9ec-0cb17e90819e"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260830-32ypr2 (final leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q) is `to-review` with checklist 14/14 and three attached outcomes. Work is uncommitted in the Story worktree on checkpoint `47294bb`; trunk stayed at `c3aae73`, so no refresh ran.\n\nWhat was built: `internal/cloneproject` — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session and Events from captured bytes. Unknown records/members become raw-addressable `opaque_event`; foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning`; foreign instructions stay low-authority history; incomplete tools resolve to aborted history with an always-empty live surface; source usage never funds target accounting; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return. AC coverage is 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests ([matrix](.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md)).\n\nEvidence: package suite green (88.9% statements, race clean); 44 narrowing mutants KILLED + control SURVIVED in each of two battery runs with per-plant logs, including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite; all 27 validation commands exit 0 (race/cover split into bounded groups; `task-board validate` shows only pre-existing warnings on unrelated tasks).\n\nStory-close: `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` bound full (2/2, 5/5) with four new acceptance cases; pin re-derived via the production marshal path (`9b9516d7…`); `tracecheck` green at cases=139, full=4, clauses 56/569 with both section runs green. `section:13.14.1` is deliberately unbound — the scanner sees zero RFC 2119 lines there (verified), so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; its record is the three TRACEABILITY files plus matrices. README, LOGBOOK, and pin tests updated with measured figures only.\n\nOne note for the orchestrator: trunk's mesh-RPC story added its own upgrade-map entries on the same base test, so integration must union both stories' entries and re-derive the pin (expected figures recorded in the results doc — re-measure, don't copy).","reason":null}}
